From d4c2439a21ffb3776d4a1e3c52c43d5b667f8826 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: cgscli <cgscli@localhost>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 10:14:35 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 13/13] P17: user-facing hints name the cgs command

Reason: A CGS build prints commands the user is meant to copy back into the terminal: `omp --resume <id>` after Ctrl+C, `omp update`, `omp plugin install`, usage lines and help examples, and the tool and prompt text the model reads. The branded binary is installed as `cgs`, so every one of them named a command that does not exist. omp already prints most of them through APP_NAME; the rest are literals.
Upstream: none (distribution-specific command name)
Remove-when: CGS stops shipping a branded omp build

- utils/dirs.ts: APP_NAME is "cgs": the help header and usage line, the `--resume` command printed on exit, the update/config/login/setup/plugin/completions messages and the process title
- the literal hints are rewritten by scripts/brand-commands.ts (in cgscli), not by hand: inline code `omp ...`, `usage: omp ...`, help examples, and `Run/Use/with omp <command>`. The product name in a sentence, `omp://`, `OMP_*`, `.omp` paths, comments and tests stay
- when this patch conflicts after an omp sync, restore the conflicting files from upstream and run `bun scripts/brand-commands.ts <omp dir>` instead of merging by hand
